# Generated by FWShift: serverd commands for a Stormshield SNS firewall (v4). Read the report first: what is
# not written is listed there. Run with: snscli --host FIREWALL --user admin --script this-file
# The script EMPTIES filter slot 9 and writes the policy there; it does not make it the active slot.
# Check that slot 9 is not the active one. Every object name starts with fws_; objects of those
# names are changed (update=1), also where an active slot uses them. snscli goes on after a command that fails:
# read its output, and run CONFIG FILTER CHECK type=filter index=9 before the slot is made active.
MODIFY FORCE ON
CONFIG OBJECT NETWORK NEW name=fws_LAN ip=10.10.0.0 mask=255.255.0.0 update=1
CONFIG OBJECT HOST NEW name=fws_192.0.2.53 ip=192.0.2.53 resolve=static update=1
